cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this benchmark, please cite it as below."
title: "plant-read-placement: placing plant specimens from noisy Nanopore reads with a plant DNA language model"
authors:
  - family-names: Odimayo
    given-names: Oluwagbade
version: 1.0.0
date-released: 2026-11-19
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/gbadedata/plant-read-placement"
abstract: >-
  A preregistered benchmark of whether a plant DNA language model (PlantCaduceus) can place a plant
  specimen as a known species, an unseen relative or likely new from a few noisy Oxford Nanopore reads,
  against k-mer composition and minimap2, on real genomes and held-out species. Targets were frozen by
  hash before a single test run.
keywords:
  - DNA language model
  - PlantCaduceus
  - Oxford Nanopore
  - species identification
  - contrastive learning
  - preregistration
  - benchmark
